    "System.Description": "<div><b>As a</b> Report Author </div><div><b>I want</b> to link one or more cells to a Discount Rate slot and have the entered value drive discounting calculations for the report </div><div><b>So that</b> I can set discount rate assumptions directly within the report template rather than configuring them elsewhere </div><div><br> </div><div><b>Size estimate:</b> TBD � shell created for estimation </div><div><b>Sequencing note:</b> None </div><div><br> </div><div><b>Requirements</b> </div><div><br> </div><div><b>Conceptual distinction from variable linking</b> </div><div>Discount Rates (Discount Settings &gt; Discount Rates) are not simple display/variable mappings � the linked cell is a live calculation input, not just a value pulled from an existing variable. This is distinct from the variable linking mechanism covered in 1869322. </div><div><br> </div><div><b>Fixed slot ceiling</b> </div><div>Discount Settings &gt; Discount Rates offers a fixed ceiling of 5 named slots (Rate 1�5). </div><div><br> </div><div><b>Many-or-few links per slot</b> </div><div>Author can create as many or as few links as needed against any of the 5 slots, including multiple links to the same slot within a template. </div><div><br> </div><div><b>Link value feeds calculation</b> </div><div>Whatever value the Author types into a linked cell is used as the actual discount rate for that Rate 1�5 slot during report generation/calculation � not just displayed. <b>Open question:</b> Marg believes this is how it works (link the slot to a cell, then type the assumption value directly into that cell) but this mechanic is not yet confirmed � verify with engineering/UAT before finalizing AC. </div>",
    "System.Id": 1869369,
